sam_cs: Heads-up: Orbit dedicated bring-up tomorrow 09:30 PT. Quota signed-off but a few loose ends: autoscale tuning, load-test windows, and a short enablement packet for customer ops. tagging @leo_infra @jin_prod @tara_oncall
leo_infra: can do. please confirm RPS shape + target p95 and i'll propose scale curve variants (reactive vs predictive).
jin_prod: expected steady-state ~150 RPS, short spikes to ~480 RPS (30-90s bursts). p95 target <= 150ms. daily quota 1.2M tokens.
sam_cs: proposal summary: reserved_pool=2xA100, burst_pool=4xA100 auto-burst, daily_quota=1_200_000, p95<=150ms. Need autoscale config and a fallback routing plan.
jin_prod: recommend min_instances=2, max_instances=14, metric=gpu_utilization, target=68%. enable prefix caching for top-10 prompt templates (reduces token work for common flows). also add model-variant fallback: compact-1 -> base-1 when queueing high.
tara_oncall: i'll run a 30m soak + 10m burst window tomorrow 10:00 PT. who can paste the locust/k6 ramp plan? i'll own traces and slow-query alerts.
sam_cs: quick k6 ramp (replace AUTH_TOKEN):
```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
export let options = { stages: [ { duration: '2m', target: 50 }, { duration: '5m', target: 150 }, { duration: '3m', target: 450 }, { duration: '10m', target: 150 } ] };
export default function() {
  http.post('https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate', JSON.stringify({input: 'probe'}), { headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer AUTH_TOKEN', 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } });
  sleep(1);
}
```
opsbot: loadtest scheduled: env=staging | job=orbit-bringup-2025-09-14 | start=2025-09-14T17:00:00Z | duration=00:30:00 | owner=tara_oncall
nisha_pm: note on renewals: Orbit's consumption has trailed forecast last quarter. After the test let's bundle the enablement playbook, usage tips (prefix caching + batch configs), and propose a joint ops review next week. I can own the calendar and customer readiness checklist (Thurs EOD).
sam_cs: action items: 1) @leo_infra produce autoscale policy + queue fallback rule; 2) @jin_prod compile cache whitelist + model fallback list; 3) @tara_oncall run soak/burst and paste metrics here; 4) @nisha_pm schedule enablement call and prep playbook. i'll update the bring-up runbook and attach canary routing.
leo_infra: on it. adding fallback rule: if avg_queue_ms > 200ms for >30s then route requests to compact-variant and open incident with prod-tag. also adding a predictive scale step using short-term moving avg of RPS to pre-warm one instance when predicted spike > 200 rps.
jin_prod: pushing cache whitelist now: endpoints using templates: ["/v1/complete","/v1/chat"] with ~35% token savings on common flows. model fallback chain: base-v2 -> compact-v1 -> tiny-v1. i'll post exact model IDs in runbook.
tara_oncall: running warmup now. will post first 10m metrics in 5. if any alarms fire i'll escalate to pager.
sam_cs: thanks team. small ask: include a one-pager for the customer ops team with steps for circuit-breaker and graceful degradation they can run if they see latency regressions. i'll draft and attach after tests. :thumbsup:
